1
00:00:03,290 --> 00:00:04,950
<i>In this world...</i>

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:10,760
<i>Is the destiny of mankind controlled by some transcendental entity or law?</i>

3
00:00:11,630 --> 00:00:14,660
<i>Is it like the hand of God hovering above?</i>

4
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,500
<i>At least it is true...</i>

5
00:00:17,940 --> 00:00:21,600
<i>...that man has no control, even over his own will.</i>

6
00:00:28,850 --> 00:00:30,210
T-This is...

7
00:00:31,080 --> 00:00:32,670
The Egg of the King!

8
00:00:42,140 --> 00:00:43,490
I see!

9
00:00:43,490 --> 00:00:45,560
So that's the ploy...

10
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,600
It's your fault...

11
00:00:48,270 --> 00:00:51,040
You put Griffith in danger
and almost got him killed...

12
00:00:51,040 --> 00:00:52,400
It's all your fault!

13
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:15,510
Feel no shame about shape

14
00:01:15,590 --> 00:01:17,430
Weather changes their phrase

15
00:01:17,550 --> 00:01:21,180
Even mother will show you another way

16
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:23,560
So put your glasses on

17
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:25,640
Nothing will be wrong

18
00:01:25,730 --> 00:01:27,850
There's no blame. There's no fame

19
00:01:27,850 --> 00:01:29,690
It's up to you

20
00:01:29,860 --> 00:01:33,320
The first words should be found

21
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,950
Whatever holds you back

22
00:01:37,820 --> 00:01:38,320
I...

23
00:01:38,700 --> 00:01:39,450
...can...

24
00:01:39,530 --> 00:01:41,620
I can get it off

25
00:01:41,620 --> 00:01:42,620
Tell me what...

26
00:01:42,620 --> 00:01:43,620
Tell me what...

27
00:01:43,620 --> 00:01:45,450
Tell me what you want

28
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:46,540
I don't know why...

29
00:01:46,750 --> 00:01:47,540
Don't know why...

30
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:49,540
Don't know why you're afraid

31
00:01:49,710 --> 00:01:50,710
Tell me what...

32
00:01:50,790 --> 00:01:51,670
Tell me what...

33
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,340
Tell me what you'd say

34
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,670
I don't know why...

35
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:55,760
Don't know why...

36
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:56,550
Too late...

37
00:01:56,630 --> 00:01:58,180
It's too late

38
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:07,100
The Sword's Owner

39
00:02:25,540 --> 00:02:28,250
Have you heard about
the Band of the Hawk?

40
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,040
I have...

41
00:02:29,040 --> 00:02:32,040
They suffered serious
losses during a recent battle.

42
00:02:32,380 --> 00:02:34,630
I can't say for certain, but...

43
00:02:34,630 --> 00:02:38,840
...soldiers claim they met some
huge demon in Tudor Castle.

44
00:02:39,180 --> 00:02:40,680
A huge demon?

45
00:02:40,890 --> 00:02:42,930
I declare it to be a falsehood...

46
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:45,470
...designed to draw attention
away from their failure.

47
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,890
It's no better than a child's trick!

48
00:02:47,890 --> 00:02:53,560
However, Griffith ultimately succeeded
in securing the castle's surrender.

49
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:57,320
Even if they did suffer serious losses,
we may not accuse them of failure.

50
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:01,740
Besides, it is rumored that
Griffith will be raised to the peerage.

51
00:03:02,240 --> 00:03:04,580
Aye, I've heard that as well.

52
00:03:04,580 --> 00:03:06,370
Really, it is true?

53
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:11,250
His reputation with the king keeps
rising due to his recent achievements.

54
00:03:11,250 --> 00:03:13,080
This is very irritating!

55
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:15,250
Why should the king give
that title to a mercenary?

56
00:03:23,930 --> 00:03:25,350
He is...

57
00:03:25,350 --> 00:03:27,310
The commander of their raiders...

58
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:34,560
You've had a terrible experience in battle.

59
00:03:35,110 --> 00:03:38,780
I heard that you encountered
a demon on the battlefield.

60
00:03:39,780 --> 00:03:43,070
I wonder if it was
the demon that injured you?

61
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:49,290
Perhaps you saw a dog in the dark
and thought it was a monster.

62
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,670
That is likely!

63
00:03:58,750 --> 00:04:00,210
Y-You...

64
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:03,430
Sorry, I'm unsteady on
my feet because of my wounds.

65
00:04:04,090 --> 00:04:05,470
D-Damn you!

66
00:04:05,470 --> 00:04:06,720
My blade hungers for you...

67
00:04:15,940 --> 00:04:17,020
Bastard...

68
00:04:38,840 --> 00:04:39,670
Guts!

69
00:04:41,460 --> 00:04:42,720
What's going on?

70
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,260
You're all out here.

71
00:04:44,260 --> 00:04:45,880
Are you well enough to walk?

72
00:04:46,180 --> 00:04:47,090
Yeah...

73
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:54,350
It's all your fault!

74
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,030
Just forget it.

75
00:05:01,030 --> 00:05:02,740
No one blames you.

76
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:06,740
Casca just said that because
she was frantic back there.

77
00:05:12,240 --> 00:05:14,370
And what are you up to?

78
00:05:15,250 --> 00:05:17,120
We want to visit Griffith.

79
00:05:17,580 --> 00:05:18,790
But...

80
00:05:18,790 --> 00:05:20,590
There are visitors here already.

81
00:05:21,250 --> 00:05:25,220
Ministers and bishops,
big shots in the royal court...

82
00:05:26,130 --> 00:05:29,180
The world is as kind
as it is cruel, so to speak.

83
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:33,850
Some of the senior statesmen
despise Griffith and regard him...

84
00:05:33,850 --> 00:05:35,980
...as an upstart mercenary commoner.

85
00:05:35,980 --> 00:05:39,650
Meanwhile, others try to gain his
favor to secure their future in the court.

86
00:05:39,650 --> 00:05:40,610
I get it...

87
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:44,320
Maybe we've just been
taking it for granted...

88
00:05:44,320 --> 00:05:47,030
...but Griffith has been invincible so far.

89
00:05:47,030 --> 00:05:50,820
Basically, he is the leader of
the strongest unit in Midland's army.

90
00:05:53,290 --> 00:05:54,040
Well, then...

91
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:55,500
Where to?

92
00:05:55,910 --> 00:05:56,710
Hey!

93
00:06:00,790 --> 00:06:01,590
Wait!

94
00:06:03,170 --> 00:06:05,260
You weren't listening, were you?

95
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,050
I was.

96
00:06:07,050 --> 00:06:07,880
So what?

97
00:06:07,880 --> 00:06:09,050
So what?

98
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:10,930
Don't give me that!

99
00:06:10,930 --> 00:06:14,720
I'm telling you to wait here until
Griffith finishes receiving his guests.

100
00:06:15,060 --> 00:06:17,100
That doesn't matter at all.

101
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:19,730
I just want to visit an injured friend.

102
00:06:19,730 --> 00:06:20,600
Guts!

103
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,610
I'm going!

104
00:06:23,650 --> 00:06:24,980
You are not allowed in!

105
00:06:24,980 --> 00:06:26,990
Please wait until the meeting is over.

106
00:06:31,450 --> 00:06:32,830
You...

107
00:06:38,040 --> 00:06:38,830
Sorry.

108
00:06:41,500 --> 00:06:42,840
Big idiot...

109
00:06:43,210 --> 00:06:45,920
Rickert, will you come with me?

110
00:06:46,210 --> 00:06:47,970
T-That's all right...

111
00:06:47,970 --> 00:06:48,760
Okay...

112
00:06:50,260 --> 00:06:51,510
Hey, Griffith...

113
00:06:52,300 --> 00:06:53,890
I'm sick of this.

114
00:06:53,890 --> 00:06:54,760
Stop trying to...

115
00:07:07,990 --> 00:07:09,570
What's the meaning of this?

116
00:07:17,830 --> 00:07:19,200
Why?

117
00:07:19,200 --> 00:07:21,670
Why are you always like this?

118
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:27,960
Why does Griffith value you so much?

119
00:07:42,900 --> 00:07:44,690
Hey, Guts!

120
00:07:44,690 --> 00:07:46,400
That spoiled everything.

121
00:07:46,400 --> 00:07:47,860
I'll come back later!

122
00:07:58,410 --> 00:07:59,540
I think...

123
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:02,370
I understand Guts's feelings somewhat.

124
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:07,290
After all, Griffith has been
unapproachable lately...

125
00:08:07,290 --> 00:08:10,300
He's been like a stranger...

126
00:08:38,080 --> 00:08:39,280
You...

127
00:08:39,620 --> 00:08:42,040
...should have been killed
by Griffith back there!

128
00:08:43,000 --> 00:08:45,710
You don't care at all about your men.

129
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:46,960
You're just a mad dog!

130
00:08:47,790 --> 00:08:48,590
Why...

131
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,170
Why are you always like this?

132
00:08:52,420 --> 00:08:53,670
It's all your fault!

133
00:08:53,670 --> 00:08:57,800
It's all your fault!

134
00:09:06,310 --> 00:09:07,600
Shit!

135
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:09,940
What the hell does she mean?

136
00:09:09,940 --> 00:09:11,020
My, you're on edge.

137
00:09:12,150 --> 00:09:13,190
Griffith.

138
00:09:13,190 --> 00:09:15,360
You seem to be able
to wield your sword...

139
00:09:15,360 --> 00:09:18,030
...despite the fact you were beaten
much more soundly than I was.

140
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,950
You are quite a tough one.

141
00:09:24,370 --> 00:09:26,330
I apologize about yesterday.

142
00:09:26,330 --> 00:09:28,830
I heard everyone came to visit me.

143
00:09:31,300 --> 00:09:33,880
Taking advantage of my injury...

144
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:38,050
...those ministers condescendingly
visit me every single day.

145
00:09:38,430 --> 00:09:40,470
To be honest, they are truly annoying.

146
00:09:41,850 --> 00:09:44,600
I'm without any choice, however.

147
00:09:54,280 --> 00:09:56,820
Nosferatu Zodd...

148
00:09:57,570 --> 00:10:01,700
To think that such an enormous
monster really exists...

149
00:10:02,280 --> 00:10:05,120
Part of me feels as if that encounter
was some kind of nightmare.

150
00:10:06,660 --> 00:10:08,920
But on the other hand...

151
00:10:08,920 --> 00:10:10,670
...it's evident such a giant exists...

152
00:10:10,670 --> 00:10:14,170
...even though it's beyond human knowledge.

153
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:16,050
I would say...

154
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:19,180
...that it might be something like a god.

155
00:10:19,180 --> 00:10:21,510
It was more like a demon, wasn't it?

156
00:10:21,510 --> 00:10:22,970
Who knows?

157
00:10:22,970 --> 00:10:24,220
It's all the same.

158
00:10:30,480 --> 00:10:33,150
By the way, how was I saved?

159
00:10:33,570 --> 00:10:36,030
I passed out in the middle of the fight.

160
00:10:36,530 --> 00:10:39,070
It was because of
that thing around your neck.

161
00:10:52,960 --> 00:11:00,970
If you and this man truly regard each
other as friends, be mindful of this...

162
00:11:03,470 --> 00:11:07,180
When this man's ambition crumbles...

163
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:12,270
...you will be destined to face your death!

164
00:11:12,270 --> 00:11:15,150
A death you can never escape!

165
00:11:16,860 --> 00:11:19,530
Zodd certainly recognized that thing...

166
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:22,780
This seems to protect me from evil.

167
00:11:23,620 --> 00:11:26,080
I've got to thank that old
fortune-teller woman.

168
00:11:30,250 --> 00:11:31,540
I think...

169
00:11:31,540 --> 00:11:33,170
I owe you again.

170
00:11:35,590 --> 00:11:36,460
Tell me why.

171
00:11:37,380 --> 00:11:38,760
Three years ago...

172
00:11:38,760 --> 00:11:42,010
...you told me that you didn't
want to lose an outstanding soldier.

173
00:11:42,300 --> 00:11:44,390
I am just a warrior serving you.

174
00:11:44,970 --> 00:11:47,470
But you were about
to lose your life for me...

175
00:11:47,470 --> 00:11:49,390
...a mere soldier.

176
00:11:49,730 --> 00:11:53,690
It's not the kind of thing that
happens to a levelheaded guy like you.

177
00:11:55,650 --> 00:11:56,690
Why?

178
00:12:02,570 --> 00:12:05,490
Oh dear, I thought we
finished up that talk three years ago.

179
00:12:05,910 --> 00:12:06,990
There's no reason...

180
00:12:06,990 --> 00:12:08,080
...in particular.

181
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:13,370
Do you want a reason?

182
00:12:15,580 --> 00:12:18,090
Do you really need a reason...

183
00:12:18,750 --> 00:12:23,680
...each time I decide to lay
my life on the line for you?

184
00:12:36,980 --> 00:12:38,940
No, I just...

185
00:12:41,530 --> 00:12:43,820
Oh, Sir White Hawk.

186
00:12:44,240 --> 00:12:46,740
You seem to have gotten better.

187
00:12:56,630 --> 00:12:57,670
Your Majesty!

188
00:12:58,500 --> 00:12:59,590
Hey, Guts!

189
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:03,880
How dare you be discourteous
in His Majesty's presence!

190
00:13:11,260 --> 00:13:13,730
Never mind that. Raise your heads.

191
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:15,230
I'm just getting some air.

192
00:13:15,230 --> 00:13:16,190
But, Your Majesty...

193
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:19,650
Everybody in the castle
has grown excited because...

194
00:13:19,650 --> 00:13:21,530
...of all the war councils.

195
00:13:21,530 --> 00:13:24,240
Alas, I do not have time
to regain my composure.

196
00:13:26,950 --> 00:13:28,410
Let me introduce you...

197
00:13:28,410 --> 00:13:30,950
This is my younger brother, Count Julius.

198
00:13:30,950 --> 00:13:35,210
He's the general of the White Dragons
and next in line to the throne.

199
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:38,500
I am Griffith.
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

200
00:13:40,540 --> 00:13:42,210
My lord Griffith...

201
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:48,300
I am always proud when you capably
lead the Band of the Hawk to victory.

202
00:13:48,840 --> 00:13:49,930
That is very kind.

203
00:13:50,140 --> 00:13:54,220
Forgetting my old age,
your dauntless courage in battle...

204
00:13:54,220 --> 00:13:57,520
...even makes me burn for a fight!

205
00:13:57,850 --> 00:14:00,270
It reminds me of those days of my youth...

206
00:14:00,270 --> 00:14:02,770
...when I worked alongside
my subjects in the war effort.

207
00:14:02,770 --> 00:14:06,950
Majesty, I must object to this
addressing of a mere unit commander.

208
00:14:06,950 --> 00:14:08,910
I do not mind talking with him.

209
00:14:09,740 --> 00:14:11,370
The truth be told...

210
00:14:11,370 --> 00:14:15,000
...some senior statesmen in the royal
court are displeased by your presence.

211
00:14:15,370 --> 00:14:17,080
Alarmed by your influence...

212
00:14:17,080 --> 00:14:18,920
...they are concerned
that your common birth...

213
00:14:18,920 --> 00:14:21,290
...might affect the prestige
of the Midland army.

214
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:26,970
However, neither prestige
nor status brings us triumph...

215
00:14:26,970 --> 00:14:28,840
...much less welfare for my people.

216
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,640
We live in a turbulent age.

217
00:14:31,600 --> 00:14:36,680
Hence, I am greatly depending upon
exceptional people like yourself...

218
00:14:36,680 --> 00:14:40,440
...rather than aristocratic generals
who are tied up in old traditions...

219
00:14:40,440 --> 00:14:44,770
...for I am committed to building
a strong foundation for my land.

220
00:14:46,780 --> 00:14:50,360
Once again, I am very much
obliged to Your Majesty.

221
00:15:00,290 --> 00:15:01,750
Who is that lady over there?

222
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:03,540
Oh...

223
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:05,920
She is my daughter, Charlotte.

224
00:15:06,710 --> 00:15:07,960
She is very shy.

225
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:10,680
According to her, she is
frightened of haughty warriors...

226
00:15:10,680 --> 00:15:13,350
...so she rarely comes out of the palace.

227
00:15:14,430 --> 00:15:16,100
Charlotte, come over here.

228
00:15:20,940 --> 00:15:22,850
She is a very private person.

229
00:15:22,850 --> 00:15:26,780
That is because she is my
only daughter, so I spoil her.

230
00:15:27,230 --> 00:15:29,280
Forgive her, Lord Griffith.

231
00:15:33,450 --> 00:15:35,580
Come along now, Charlotte.

232
00:15:55,220 --> 00:15:56,350
Pardon me.

233
00:15:56,350 --> 00:15:57,560
Be careful, my lady.

234
00:16:01,890 --> 00:16:02,940
You bastard!

235
00:16:03,400 --> 00:16:06,230
Such discourtesy,
touching the princess's body!

236
00:16:07,570 --> 00:16:08,730
Hey, old man!

237
00:16:13,910 --> 00:16:15,410
Pardon my improper manner...

238
00:16:16,200 --> 00:16:18,370
...Your Excellency Julius.

239
00:16:22,830 --> 00:16:24,420
What's keeping you?

240
00:16:24,870 --> 00:16:28,210
Oh, it's nothing, Father.

241
00:16:29,460 --> 00:16:31,210
We shall go, my lady.

242
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:15,760
Do you really need a reason...

243
00:17:15,760 --> 00:17:19,550
...each time I decide to lay
my life on the line for you?

244
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:23,060
He said, "For you"...

245
00:17:30,770 --> 00:17:34,030
I don't know if this is the answer
I've been looking for all my life.

246
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:39,570
But for now...

247
00:17:40,950 --> 00:17:44,040
I will fight with my sword for him!

248
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:24,370
All right, everyone!

249
00:18:24,620 --> 00:18:27,370
Do you understand how
important this stronghold is?

250
00:18:27,580 --> 00:18:28,540
No, sir!

251
00:18:28,540 --> 00:18:29,580
Idiots!

252
00:18:29,580 --> 00:18:31,500
You should know your history!

253
00:18:32,170 --> 00:18:36,340
Listen, due to our capture of Doldrey,
for the first time we were able...

254
00:18:36,340 --> 00:18:38,840
...to successfully split the enemy lines.

255
00:18:39,130 --> 00:18:42,050
Afterwards, this stronghold
was built as our army's...

256
00:18:42,050 --> 00:18:44,810
...staging point for attacks against Midland.

257
00:18:46,140 --> 00:18:47,180
Behold this road!

258
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:51,060
This road once functioned as the
most important pass for military troops...

259
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,230
...between Doldrey and
the kingdom's territory.

260
00:18:53,820 --> 00:18:56,610
However, since our military
forces seized this bridge...

261
00:18:56,610 --> 00:18:58,780
...the tide of the war turned.

262
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,240
They were forced...

263
00:19:01,240 --> 00:19:04,990
...to expose the heart of Midland
directly before our military forces.

264
00:19:05,620 --> 00:19:07,200
According to the secret tactics...

265
00:19:07,200 --> 00:19:10,420
...handed down
the Coborlwitz family for 300 years...

266
00:19:10,420 --> 00:19:13,040
...capture a road and you will capture victory.

267
00:19:15,550 --> 00:19:18,880
To capture victory,
we should strengthen our defenses...

268
00:19:21,760 --> 00:19:23,720
My defense is already planned!

269
00:19:24,550 --> 00:19:25,260
Look...

270
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,890
If the enemy attacks us,
they have to march over this bridge.

271
00:19:29,850 --> 00:19:33,480
Therefore, the best soldiers from
the garrison will amass on the bridge.

272
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:35,570
It's a narrow stone bridge...

273
00:19:35,570 --> 00:19:38,110
...so only a mounted soldier
or two can charge at a time.

274
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:40,570
Moreover, Tudor's best crossbowmen...

275
00:19:40,570 --> 00:19:43,530
...will be standing by
above the exterior gate.

276
00:19:43,530 --> 00:19:47,870
Our crossbowmen will definitely
cut down the enemy leaders...

277
00:19:47,870 --> 00:19:49,290
...as they march one by one.

278
00:19:49,950 --> 00:19:51,000
It's perfect!

279
00:19:51,500 --> 00:19:53,370
We'll deliver a severe blow to the enemy...

280
00:19:53,370 --> 00:19:56,090
...and thanks to my fantastic scheme,
we'll escape any damage!

281
00:19:56,380 --> 00:19:58,210
You can trust me on this!

282
00:19:58,670 --> 00:20:04,090
But what if the enemy doesn't use
this bridge and attacks our flanks?

283
00:20:05,600 --> 00:20:06,850
You need not worry.

284
00:20:07,430 --> 00:20:11,060
There is no bridge or ford along
the river within eight miles of here.

285
00:20:11,520 --> 00:20:15,860
And the river is so wide and deep that
even the best horse could not cross.

286
00:20:16,230 --> 00:20:19,820
B-But what if the enemy
makes a raft, and...

287
00:20:21,690 --> 00:20:24,410
As you can see, we are in a barren
land of rocks and vineyards.

288
00:20:24,410 --> 00:20:26,870
It is impossible to make rafts
because there aren't enough trees.

289
00:20:27,330 --> 00:20:30,500
Even if the enemy made what
they could with the nearby trees...

290
00:20:30,500 --> 00:20:33,830
...they wouldn't be able to send
enough of their troops over at once.

291
00:20:35,830 --> 00:20:39,300
Or will they make rafts
out of the grapevines?

292
00:20:55,940 --> 00:20:59,360
Why do we have to sortie
the minute Griffith gets better?

293
00:20:59,360 --> 00:21:02,030
They depend on us in battle.

294
00:21:02,690 --> 00:21:04,070
But didn't they say...

295
00:21:04,530 --> 00:21:08,530
...even the heavily equipped Golem
Knights failed to capture that castle?

296
00:21:08,990 --> 00:21:11,040
I heard they suffered severely.

297
00:21:11,490 --> 00:21:15,960
Reportedly, two thirds of the knights
were defeated on the bridge.

298
00:21:15,960 --> 00:21:17,750
What, are you serious?

299
00:21:39,690 --> 00:21:41,570
It's our turn.

300
00:21:41,570 --> 00:21:42,860
We'll dispose of them.

301
00:22:03,390 --> 00:22:05,850
Looking back, the morning comes.

302
00:22:05,850 --> 00:22:09,350
Don't find your face in your glass.

303
00:22:10,390 --> 00:22:13,480
Take the moonlight by the tail.

304
00:22:13,480 --> 00:22:16,440
It's a rainy sight. You're shading.

305
00:22:17,900 --> 00:22:19,650
What is that?

306
00:22:19,650 --> 00:22:20,900
It's just the same.

307
00:22:20,900 --> 00:22:24,070
What is trying your crown?

308
00:22:25,160 --> 00:22:28,370
I'm spending my glass, walking back.

309
00:22:28,370 --> 00:22:31,410
So wear my glass. You're fading.

310
00:22:31,710 --> 00:22:51,310
I'm waiting so long.

311
00:22:51,310 --> 00:23:00,400
I'm waiting...

